{"type":"message","id":"2deaa6be","parentId":"05e7237a","timestamp":"2026-05-23T04:23:53.988Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The tool isn't available as a direct Node module. Let me use the sessions_send to route to the feishu tool, or check if there's a proper way to call it. Actually, looking at the system prompt, I should be calling the `feishu_wiki` tool directly as a function - but it seems like the tool definitions are abstractions that need to go through OpenClaw's tool routing system.\n\nWait, I think the issue is I'm trying to call the feishu tools directly via require but they don't exist as a direct module path. Let me check if there's a gateway tool or config action I can use.\n\nActually looking at the SKILL.md for feishu-wiki, it says \"Single tool `feishu_wiki`\" - this suggests it should be called as a tool, not as a Node module. But in the current session, I only have access to specific tools (exec, read, write, edit, etc.). \n\nLet me look at how to actually call feishu_wiki. Looking at the config schema, there might be a `gateway` tool for calling provider-specific tools. Let me check what's available.\n\nActually, looking at the OpenClaw docs more carefully - when it says \"Single tool `feishu_wiki`\" in the SKILL, it means the feishu plugin registers a tool of that name, and I should be able to call it through the normal tool calling mechanism. But I don't see it in my available tools list. \n\nThe tools I see are: read, write, edit, exec, process, web_search, web_fetch, cron, sessions_list, sessions_history, sessions_send, sessions_spawn, sessions_yield, subagents, session_status, image, image_generate, music_generate, update_plan, video_generate, memory_get, memory_search\n\nI don't see feishu_wiki or feishu_doc in this list. This means either:\n1. The tools aren't loaded/available in this session\n2. They might be available through a different mechanism\n\nLet me check the gateway tool and see if ther